 ```
 
 ## API
 
-Every body is JSON. A task is `{ "id": 1, "title": "Buy milk", "done": false, "created_at": "2026-01-31T09:00:00.000Z" }`.
+Every body is JSON. A task is `{ "id": 1, "title": "Buy milk", "done": false, "created_at": "2026-01-31T09:00:00.000Z", "tags": ["home"] }`.
+`tags` is always an array of strings sorted alphabetically, `[]` when the task has none.
 
 | Method and path | What it does | Answers |
 |---|---|---|
-| `GET /api/tasks` | Lists the tasks, oldest first; `?done=true` or `?done=false` keeps the done or the open ones | 200, an array of tasks |
-| `POST /api/tasks` | Creates a task from `{ "title": "…" }` | 201, the task |
+| `GET /api/tasks` | Lists the tasks, oldest first; `?done=true` or `?done=false` keeps the done or the open ones; `?tag=home` keeps the tasks with that tag; both combine | 200, an array of tasks, or 400 `{ "error": "invalid done" }` for any other `done` value |
+| `GET /api/tags` | Lists the tags in use with their number of tasks, sorted by name: `[{ "name": "home", "count": 2 }]`; a tag no task uses is not listed | 200, an array |
+| `POST /api/tasks` | Creates a task from `{ "title": "…", "tags": ["home"] }` (`tags` is optional) | 201, the task, or 400 `{ "error": "invalid tags" }` |
 | `GET /api/tasks/:id` | Reads a task | 200, or 404 `{ "error": "task not found" }` |
-| `PATCH /api/tasks/:id` | Changes `title` and / or `done` | 200, the task, or 404 |
+| `PATCH /api/tasks/:id` | Changes `title`, `done` and / or `tags`; `tags` replaces the whole list (`[]` clears it), and leaving it out keeps the tags | 200, the task, 400 `{ "error": "invalid tags" }`, or 404 |
 | `DELETE /api/tasks/:id` | Deletes a task | 204, or 404 |
 
 Errors answer `{ "error": "<message>" }`.
 
+### Tags
+
+Tags are normalized first: trimmed, lowercased, duplicates removed. A valid tag is 1 to 30 characters among `a-z`,
+`0-9` and `-`, and a task has at most 10 tags (counted after removing duplicates). `tags` must be an array of strings;
+anything else, or a tag that breaks these rules, answers 400 `{ "error": "invalid tags" }` and nothing changes (no task
+is created, none is updated). `?tag=` takes a name normalized the same way; a name that is not a valid tag matches no
+task and answers `[]`. Deleting a task removes its links to tags.
+
 ## Layout
 
-- `src/db.ts`: opens the database and runs the migrations (`PRAGMA user_version` counts those applied).
+- `src/db.ts`: opens the database and runs the migrations (`PRAGMA user_version` counts those applied). Tables:
+  `tasks`, `tags` (`id`, unique `name`) and `task_tags` (`task_id`, `tag_id`, both `ON DELETE CASCADE`).
 - `src/tasks.ts`: the queries.
 - `src/app.ts`: the HTTP server and its routes.
 - `public/`: the page.
 - `test/`: the API tests, against a server on a random port with an in-memory database.
